'''Mithel''', nicknamed "'''Mauler''',"<ref name="X-wing 2" /> was a [[human]]<ref name="USW" /> individual who served a [[pilot]] in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Starfighter Corps]], flying as [[Black Two]] within [[Black Squadron (Galactic Empire)|Black Squadron]].<ref name="X-wing 2" />

At the battle, the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebels]] attacked the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|DS-1 Death Star Mobile Battle Station]] and Vader ordered [["Backstabber"|Backstabber]] and Mithel to be his wingmen. Vader followed [[Red Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Red Squadron]] which was targeting a [[thermal exhaust port]],<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> which was a flaw designed by the Imperial scientist [[Galen Walton Erso]] so that the Rebel Alliance could exploit this vulnerability and destroy the battle station itself.<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Vader shot many Rebel pilots until only Luke Skywalker remained to target the port. Suddenly, the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' piloted by Han Solo appeared and shot Backstabber, killing him. The destruction of his TIE fighter shocked Vader as Mithel tried to maneuver but accidentally flew over Vader, damaging the [[Darth Vader's TIE Advanced|Sith Lord's TIE Advanced x1]] and crashing his TIE fighter into a wall. Vader and his damaged [[TIE Advanced x1]] flew away, damaged and incapacitated. Luke Skywalker destroyed the Death Star after both of his accompanying wingmen fell.<ref name="Episode IV" />

